    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0379" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.74/50: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-03T16:00:00-00:44"><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>23. Your telegram number 18. Interview with the President requested but [I was]
                    informed that he is ill and not strong enough to take up office duties, will see
                    me as soon as conditions permit. Refer to my despatch number 91 due at New York
                    City <hi rendition="#italic">Berengaria</hi> today or tomorrow.<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d217-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
